    </TimelineContent>
  </TimelineItem>
</Timeline>`,
  preview: "canvas",
  previewLabel: "Actor, action, time, and object entries joined by the rail",
  docs: {
    purpose: [
      "Timeline shows who did what, when — an ordered feed of events with a gutter marker per entry and a rail connecting consecutive entries.",
      "The parts mirror the anatomy: Timeline is the list, TimelineItem one entry, TimelineContent the text column, TimelineHeader the description-plus-time row, TimelineTime the relative timestamp.",
      "The rail is component-owned CSS: every item draws it and the last item hides it, so callers never mark the final entry.",
    ],
    useWhen: [
      "Recent activity, audit history, or any event stream ordered by time.",
      "Each entry names an actor and an action, optionally linking to the object it touched.",
    ],
    avoidWhen: [
      "Rows share a column structure readers compare — that is a Table.",
      "There are no events to show; render Empty instead of an empty feed.",
      "The content is messages in a conversation; that is a different composition.",
    ],
    rules: [
      {
        title: "Items own the rail",
        description:
          "TimelineItem draws the connector to the next entry and hides it on the last item via group-last. Never thread an is-last flag through data.",
      },
      {
        title: "The gutter marker is composed",
        description:
          "Compose an Avatar (size md) as the item's first child. The rail offsets are tuned to that marker.",
      },
      {
        title: "Header text truncates, time never wraps",
        description:
          "The description composes Text with min-w-0 flex-1; TimelineTime is shrink-0 so the timestamp stays whole.",
      },
      {
        title: "Objects are Links",
        description:
          "The touched object under the header composes Link (tone default, body-md), not a click handler.",
      },
    ],
    accessibility: [
      "Timeline renders a real <ol> and items are <li>, so assistive technology announces entry count and position.",
      "The connector rail is decorative and aria-hidden.",
      "Entry meaning lives in visible text and real links; no ARIA additions are needed.",
    ],
    composition: [
      "Author TimelineItems directly inside Timeline in chronological order.",
      "Inside an item: the marker first, then TimelineContent with TimelineHeader (Text + TimelineTime) and the object Link.",
      "Page placement (px-5 py-5 in the admin rail) is caller classes on Timeline.",
    ],
    agentNotes: [
      "There is no is-last, variant, or orientation prop anywhere in this family; the parts are the API.",
      "Do not wrap items in extra elements between Timeline and TimelineItem — the rail's group-last relies on items being siblings.",
      "Keep descriptions one line: actor in a strong tag, verb after it.",
    ],
    props: [
      { name: "Timeline.children", type: "node", description: "The TimelineItems in order." },
      {
        name: "Timeline.classes",
        type: "string",
        description: "Layout classes for page placement.",
      },
      {
        name: "Timeline.id",
        type: "string",
        description: "Optional identifier applied to the list.",
      },
      {
        name: "TimelineItem.children",
        type: "node",
        description: "The gutter marker, then TimelineContent.",
      },
      {
        name: "TimelineItem.classes",
        type: "string",
        description: "Exceptional composition classes on the entry.",
      },
      {
        name: "TimelineItem.id",
        type: "string",
        description: "Optional identifier applied to the entry.",
      },
      {
        name: "TimelineContent.children",
        type: "node",
        description: "TimelineHeader and the composed body.",
      },
      {
        name: "TimelineContent.classes",
        type: "string",
        description: "Exceptional composition classes on the text column.",
      },
      {
        name: "TimelineContent.id",
        type: "string",
        description: "Optional identifier applied to the column.",
      },
      {
        name: "TimelineHeader.children",
        type: "node",
        description: "Description Text and TimelineTime.",
      },
      {
        name: "TimelineHeader.classes",
        type: "string",
        description: "Exceptional composition classes on the header row.",
      },
      {
        name: "TimelineHeader.id",
        type: "string",
        description: "Optional identifier applied to the row.",
      },
      { name: "TimelineTime.children", type: "node", description: "The relative timestamp text." },
      {
        name: "TimelineTime.classes",
        type: "string",
        description: "Exceptional composition classes on the timestamp.",
      },
      {
